./../docs/phase-02-safety/README.md), retain signal/timer/retry/idempotency/compensation and tool failure records; exact replay consumes recorded model/tool outputs, while audit policy retains digests, schemas, decisions, review events and providers. None is allowed only in interactive or non-safe contexts; workflow and release claims require replay or audit. Execute retention/deletion and secret-tainted memory denial fixtures through the declared provider; prompt text never grants authority. Residual criterion runtime/hot-reload-invalidation: For a changed interactive definition, record changed source, affected namespace/dependency edges and invalidation of stale syntax, analysis, typed core, MIR/domain IR, backend, runtime and package artifacts. Emit a hot-reload/session record distinguishing preserved runtime state from state that must restart, with evaluated-form/source/generated-origin identity. Show an unaffected artifact retained and affected artifacts rebuilt or rejected before reuse; reject a stale analysis/MIR/backend/runtime/package artifact, untracked build-affecting state and debug inspection outside grants/secret policy. Build-affecting session inputs are captured or explicitly nonhermetic; interactive manifests do not imply release runtime support. Build-affecting sessions emit transcripts, evaluated-form artifacts, syntax/core/MIR snapshots, dependency invalidation records and source maps; debug hooks cannot expose raw memory, host process state or model/tool outputs without grants.",
   :source-sha256
