   :criterion
   "Select debug services explicitly for each native/managed runtime and release policy. Show a debug artifact and release artifact whose service/helper manifests expose exactly the selected stack/allocation/check/trace hooks; debug-only services are absent in release unless policy explicitly allows and marks them. Preserve source/check/allocation/provider/lifetime/release identity and proof-elision metadata. Stack diagnostics are capability-neutral unless an external lookup is enabled: reject undeclared filesystem, environment, network or symbol-server access, unmarked debug services and lost source/provenance; required safety checks cannot disappear with debug instrumentation. Provider debug manifests retain profile support, allocation effects, layout/alignment, failure/lifetime/deallocation strategy and unsafe boundaries; traces retain allocation site, resource ID and release site, including selected borrow-debug checks. Enforce sink grants and redact secrets, credentials, prompts, model outputs, user/tainted inputs, raw memory, environment values, package tokens, database rows and deployment identifiers; local logging permission cannot authorize network telemetry.",
