   :criterion
   "At each claimed host adapter, manifest host/Gravity representation and nullability and convert host null or undefined through the selected Option, Result, checked-wrapper or opaque-foreign-value contract. Execute null, undefined and non-null fixtures for that declared boundary, retaining taint, errors and source/generated-origin diagnostics. Reject unchecked host null/undefined entering a safe Gravity value, a conversion inconsistent with its Gravity type or a missing adapter/null policy; an opaque foreign value does not authorize unchecked access or leakage into lower profiles. Alternative conversion policies are conditional choices, not a requirement to apply every conversion to one value. Exception/null boundary fixtures also reject untranslated host exceptions or rejected promises and preserve the declared Gravity error/panic/effect channel.",
