   :criterion
   "Have backend, package, observability, conformance and self-hosting consumers read the emitted runtime manifest and cross-check it against the actual selected service/helper/provider graph. Emit consumer agreement evidence for family/profile/target, service classification, linked support objects, generated helpers, delegated typed adapters, external providers, forbidden services, capability enforcement hooks or static proofs, startup/initialization/cleanup/failure policy and runtime diagnostic schema/provenance. Reject an absent/unreadable manifest, omitted or contradictory service/provider, hidden forbidden dependency, missing enforcement hook/proof or lost artifact/source-origin edge. A manifest link or producer-only record cannot establish consumer integration. Native backend integration includes C and LLVM artifacts for the claimed target matrix; fixture inspection alone does not claim those targets implemented.",
